§ `s 278.98 -- Reasons in certain proceedings`

-- The offences by section number (seam rule R1): 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160(2), 160(3), 170 to 173, 271 to 273.
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 151
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 152, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 152
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 153, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 153
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 153.1, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 153.1
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 155, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 155
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(2)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "subsection 160(2)"
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(3)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or (3)"
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(1)") EQUALS NOTHING   -- 160(1) is not named
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 170, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 170
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 173, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 173
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 174, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- 174 follows the named range
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 169, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- 169 precedes it
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 271, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 271
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 273, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 273
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 273.1, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- 273.1 is not named
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 270, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- 270 is not named
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the offence is one of those the subsection names` (`Provision of the Code` OF 152.5, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- between 152 and 153

#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1)(a) acquitted` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1)(b) found guilty` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1)(c) discharged, after having been found guilty` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1)(d) found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1)(e) found unfit to stand trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(1) the decision is one of those the subsection names` `s 278.98(1) a decision of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another decision (a stay, say)

#ASSERT `s 278.98(2) subsection (1) also applies to the proceedings for the historical offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both conditions
#ASSERT `s 278.98(2) subsection (1) also applies to the proceedings for the historical offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the conduct would not be an offence referred to in (1)
#ASSERT `s 278.98(2) subsection (1) also applies to the proceedings for the historical offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an offence "as it read from time to time before the day"

#ASSERT `s 278.98(4) section 278.98 applies to the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before a judge without a jury
#ASSERT `s 278.98(4) section 278.98 applies to the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "applies only" before a judge without a jury

-- Argument order of the composition: the answer of (1) as to the offence; of (2); of (1) as to the decision; of (4).
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a named offence, a named decision, a judge alone
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a historical offence within (2)
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a jury trial: "applies only in proceedings before a judge without a jury"
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither (1) nor (2) names the offence
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a decision of another kind
#ASSERT `s 278.98 the judge shall provide reasons for the decision` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- subsection (4)'s answer not determined

#ASSERT `s 278.98(3) the way the reasons are given` TRUE EQUALS `s 278.98(3) the reasons are entered in the record of the proceedings`   -- recorded proceedings: entered in the record
#ASSERT `s 278.98(3) the way the reasons are given` FALSE EQUALS `s 278.98(3) the reasons are provided in writing`   -- "if the proceedings are not recorded, shall be provided in writing"

#TRACE `s 278.98(1) the duty to provide reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 278.98(1) provide reasons for the decision` AT 4
